# mod-auto-loot: the player's own switch (the /fl hub's Settings, Chris 2026-10-31), `.autoloot on|off`,
# kept per character. Off: the bot's own kill keeps its loot; on again: the same corpse is looted at the
# next scan; off survives a relog. "Squealer" Thornmantle (3229) drops Squealer's Tusk 4951 at 100 %.
name    Auto loot - the player's switch: off loots nothing, on loots again, kept over a relog
timeout 90s

bot k warrior slot=6
group none

place 1 -3104.0 -1205.0 85.6 0
require k alive
do k destroy 4951
as k .autoloot off
expect output has "Auto-Loot is off"
pick b creature:3229 near k alive
require b exists
# the director has auto-loot too: out of reach (40 yd)
do gm goto -3104.0 -1245.0 85.6
do k approach b
do k attack b
waitfor b dead timeout 20s
wait 3s
expect k item 4951 == 0

as k .autoloot on
expect output has "Auto-Loot is on"
waitfor k item 4951 >= 1 timeout 5s

as k .autoloot off
do k relog
waitfor k exists timeout 20s
as k .autoloot
expect output has "Auto-Loot is off"

cleanup
as k .autoloot on
do k stop
do k destroy 4951
